<!--
  The AR depth scan's reference output, used by the core's obstacle tests.

  This is the shape both shells write to <staging>/obstacles.xml: a complete
  MJCF document whose <worldbody> holds the scanned boxes directly (no
  <body> wrapper), each at its absolute world position. The core strips the
  outer <mujoco>/<worldbody> and merges the geom entries into the scene.

  Contract:
    * geom type="box"; size="half-x half-y half-z" in metres;
    * pos = the box's centre in world coordinates;
    * condim="3", the floor's own;
    * <= 3 geoms (the shells cap the scan);
    * a body-less geom under worldbody is static — no joint, no qpos.

  This one is a 0.20 x 0.40 x 0.10 m piece of furniture raised 0.05 m
  (centre z = 0.05, top at 0.10 m) 0.40 m in front of the duck. The duck
  faces +x in the official MJCF; its trunk starts at x = 0.
-->
<mujoco model="duck-depth-obstacles">
  <worldbody>
    <geom name="depth_obstacle_0" type="box" size="0.10 0.20 0.05"
          pos="0.4 0 0.05" condim="3"/>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>